<section class="band" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="shell promise">
    <div class="mos-panel">
      <span class="ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-lock"/></svg></span>
      <h3 class="mos-card-title">Own your data</h3>
      <p class="mos-meta">It lives on a machine you control — at home or on a server you rent — and only you hold the keys. Nobody mines it, nobody sells it, and you can walk away with all of it whenever you like.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mos-panel">
      <span class="ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-check"/></svg></span>
      <h3 class="mos-card-title">Simple like an app store</h3>
      <p class="mos-meta">Set it up once. From then on, adding an app is like installing one on your phone: pick it, tap Install, open it. The database, the address and the padlock are handled for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mos-panel">
      <span class="ico"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg></span>
      <h3 class="mos-card-title">Privacy you can verify</h3>
      <p class="mos-meta">MOS has no telemetry and never reports back to us. Every app in the catalog is privacy-graded before it gets in, with the evidence published, so you know what an app sends out before you install it.</p>
